   "notes": "Describes the LLaMA family (7B/13B/33B/65B from Table 2); the block ops use the 7B values. The FFN hidden size is given only as a formula (\"$\\frac23 4d$ instead of $4d$\"), with no integer per model, so d_ff and the gate/up widths are left not_stated. The paper states none of these, so they are not_stated: head_dim, n_kv_heads, vocab size (BPE/SentencePiece is mentioned with no size), context length, norm eps, rope theta and pairing, biases, embedding tying, and a final norm before the head. No final norm op is emitted because the paper does not mention one. Residual and sequential (non-parallel) sublayers are marked inherited from the original Transformer, based on the paper's statement that it lists only the differences from that architecture. Bias and tying values are deliberately not inherited from the original Transformer."
  },
